WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:04.922
Compare day one with day two:
one new, eleven persisting,

3
00:00:04.922 --> 00:00:07.963
one resolved, and both changes are Erin's.

4
00:00:07.963 --> 00:00:11.550
Her Entra finding resolved;
a SailPoint finding opened.

5
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.402
Then run the re-read
client offline over six

6
00:00:14.402 --> 00:00:17.175
waiting records at noon on November first.

7
00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:20.563
Erin's record verifies, and
would be patched to closed.

8
00:00:20.563 --> 00:00:23.856
One record is pending: a
terminated user's account,

9
00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.587
read before the finding started waiting.

10
00:00:26.587 --> 00:00:29.237
One is skipped for an
empty intended state.

11
00:00:29.237 --> 00:00:31.206
Run the same records a day later,

12
00:00:31.206 --> 00:00:34.763
and that pending one becomes
a mismatch, and would reopen.

13
00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:36.575
Everything here is a dry run.

14
00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:40.638
The offline mode refuses the
apply flag, and a subject with no

15
00:00:40.638 --> 00:00:44.700
saved read is an error, because
a missing read is never a match.

16
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.496
On a developer instance,

17
00:00:46.496 --> 00:00:51.050
Chapter 5's Lab 2 runs the same
client for real, as the verifier.
